{
 "_about": "Every third-party component this repository ships or depends on: its source, version and licence (NSOT_STAGE10_PLAN 8.2a, the operator, 2026-10-04). tests/test_third_party_inventory.py holds it to the repository: every tracked file is claimed (third-party or own), every requirement has an entry, and every licence is approved or reviewed. A new component without an entry fails CI. Licences are SPDX expressions, reviewed by a person from each component's declared metadata; the vendored front-end files' versions and sources agree with static/js/vendor/MANIFEST.json.",
 "approved": {
  "0BSD": "permissive, no conditions",
  "Apache-2.0": "permissive, with a patent grant; keep its NOTICE where one exists",
  "BSD-2-Clause": "permissive; keep the copyright notice",
  "BSD-3-Clause": "permissive; keep the copyright notice",
  "ISC": "permissive; keep the copyright notice",
  "LicenseRef-Public-Domain": "no conditions",
  "MIT": "permissive; keep the copyright and permission notice",
  "OFL-1.1": "fonts: may be bundled with software; never sold on their own",
  "PSF-2.0": "permissive; keep the notice"
 },
 "reviewed": {
  "LGPL-2.1-or-later": "paramiko and scp, used unmodified as separately installed Python libraries (pip, not copied into the repository), so this project's own licence is not constrained. A modified copy, or one bundled into a single artefact, would need its source offered: the release's Docker image ships them as installed packages with their licence files (the audit confirms)",
  "MPL-2.0": "bidict and certifi, used unmodified as installed libraries. MPL is file-level copyleft: only a change to their own files would have to be shared",
  "LicenseRef-MIB-derived": "deploy/snmp_exporter/routing-modules.yml is GENERATED by prom/snmp-generator from IETF MIBs (the IETF Trust's BSD terms) and Cisco's CISCO-SMI and CISCO-BGP4-MIB. It carries the MIBs' DESCRIPTION text as metric help. The release audit decides: keep, or regenerate without the Cisco MIBs' text"
 },
